["Here is an example of how you might implement such a function in C using POSIX threads (pthreads) and semaphores. This code does not include all the features mentioned, but it provides a starting point for creating a dynamic pool of semaphores that can be resized dynamically based on demand patterns:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <semaphore.h>

typedef struct SemaphorePool {
    sem_t *semaphores;
    int size;
    pthread_mutex_t mutex;
} SemaphorePool;

SemaphorePool* createSemaphorePool(int initialSize) {
    SemaphorePool *pool = malloc(sizeof(SemaphorePool));
    pool->semaphores = malloc(initialSize * sizeof(sem_t));
    for (int i = 0; i < initialSize; i++) {
        sem_init(&pool->semaphores[i], 0, 1);
    }
    pool->size = initialSize;
    pthread_mutex_init(&pool->mutex, NULL);
    return pool;
}

void resizeSemaphorePool(SemaphorePool *pool, int newSize) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&pool->mutex);
    if (newSize > pool->size) {
        pool->semaphores = realloc(pool->semaphores, newSize * sizeof(sem_t));
        for (int i = pool->size; i < newSize; i++) {
            sem_init(&pool->semaphores[i], 0, 1);
        }
    } else if (newSize < pool->size) {
        for (int i = newSize; i < pool->size; i++) {
            sem_destroy(&pool->semaphores[i]);
        }
        pool->semaphores = realloc(pool->semaphores, newSize * sizeof(sem_t));
    }
    pool->size = newSize;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&pool->mutex);
}

void destroySemaphorePool(SemaphorePool *pool) {
    for (int i = 0; i < pool->size; i++) {
        sem_destroy(&pool->semaphores[i]);
    }
    free(pool->semaphores);
    pthread_mutex_destroy(&pool->mutex);
    free(pool);
}
```
This code creates a pool of semaphores, resizes the pool dynamically, and destroys the pool when it's no longer needed. It uses a mutex to ensure thread safety during resize operations. 

Please note that this is a simplified example and does not include all the features mentioned in your request. For instance, it doesn't integrate with an external configuration service or provide logging mechanisms for semaphore usage and performance metrics. Also, it assumes that the demand patterns are known and can be used to dynamically resize the pool. In a real-world application, you would likely need to use more sophisticated methods to estimate demand patterns and adjust the size of the pool accordingly.
"]

