['Here is a simplified version of the code that meets your requirements. This is not a complete solution but it gives you an idea about how to start implementing such a system in Java. 

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

public class ServiceManager {
    private final Map<String, Service> services = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public void startService(String serviceId) {
        Service service = services.get(serviceId);
        if (service != null && service.isPaused()) {
            service.resume();
        } else {
            service = new Service(serviceId);
            services.put(serviceId, service);
            service.start();
        }
    }

    public void stopService(String serviceId) {
        Service service = services.get(serviceId);
        if (service != null && !service.isStopped()) {
            service.stop();
        }
    }

    public void pauseService(String serviceId) {
        Service service = services.get(serviceId);
        if (service != null && !service.isPaused() && !service.isStopped()) {
            service.pause();
        }
    }

    // Other methods for managing streams, dependencies, etc...
}

class Service extends Thread {
    private final String id;
    private volatile boolean running = true;
    private volatile boolean paused = false;

    public Service(String id) {
        this.id = id;
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (running && !Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) {
            if (!paused) {
                // Perform service operations...
            } else {
                synchronized(this) {
                    try {
                        wait();
                    } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    public void pause() {
        paused = true;
    }

    public synchronized void resume() {
        paused = false;
        notifyAll();
    }

    public void stop() {
        running = false;
        resume(); // Unblock if paused
        interrupt(); // Interrupt the thread
    }

    public boolean isPaused() {
        return paused;
    }

    public boolean isStopped() {
        return !running;
    }
}
```
This code creates a `ServiceManager` that manages multiple services. Each service runs in its own thread and can be paused, resumed or stopped independently. The `Service` class uses the wait/notify mechanism to pause and resume operations. 

