['Here is an example implementation using Java's built-in `ClassLoader`, `Gson` for JSON parsing, and a simple cache mechanism with `HashMap`. This code does not include error handling for dependencies as it would require more specific information about how to handle these cases. 

```java
import com.google.gson.*;
import java.lang.reflect.*;
import java.util.*;

public class ComponentLoader {
    private static final Gson gson = new Gson();
    private static final Map<String, Object> cache = new HashMap<>();

    public <T> T loadComponent(String jsonMetadata, Class<T> interfaceType) throws Exception {
        JsonObject metadata = gson.fromJson(jsonMetadata, JsonObject.class);

        String className = metadata.get("className").getAsString();
        String version = metadata.get("version").getAsString();
        List<Dependency> dependencies = gson.fromJson(metadata.get("dependencies"), new TypeToken<List<Dependency>>(){}.getType());

        // Check if component is in cache
        Object cachedComponent = cache.get(className);
        if (cachedComponent != null && interfaceType.isInstance(cachedComponent)) {
            return interfaceType.cast(cachedComponent);
        }

        Class<?> clazz = ClassLoader.getSystemClassLoader().loadClass(className);

        // Check if class is assignable to the specified interface and has the correct version
        if (!interfaceType.isAssignableFrom(clazz) || !version.equals(clazz.getPackage().getImplementationVersion())) {
            throw new Exception("Invalid component class or version");
        }

        // Check dependencies (not implemented in this example)

        Constructor<?> constructor = clazz.getConstructor();
        Object instance = constructor.newInstance();

        cache.put(className, instance);

        return interfaceType.cast(instance);
    }

    private static class Dependency {
        String className;
        String version;

        public Dependency(String className, String version) {
            this.className = className;
            this.version = version;
        }
    }
}
```
This code assumes that the JSON metadata includes a `className` field with the fully qualified class name of the component, a `version` field with the expected version of the component, and a `dependencies` field containing an array of objects each having `className` and `version` fields. 

Please note that this code does not handle dependencies or provide error messages for cases where they cannot be met. Also, it assumes that the class name is always fully qualified and that the version is stored in the implementation version attribute of the package. These assumptions may need to be adjusted based on your specific requirements.
