        context = malloc(sizeof(NR_DL_FRAME_TRANSPORT_CONTEXT*));
        *context = NULL;  // Initialize to NULL

        // Set the thread-local storage value
        pthread_setspecific(thread_local_storage, context);
    }

    // Add new frames, update existing ones, and safely clean up resources as needed...
}
```
This code uses `pthread_key_create` to create a key for thread-local storage. The value associated with this key is a pointer to the dynamic array of structures. When a thread first calls `initializeAndManageDynamicArray`, it allocates memory for its own copy of the dynamic array and sets it as the thread-local storage value using `pthread_setspecific`. Subsequent calls from the same thread will retrieve this value with `pthread_getspecific`.

