["Here's a basic implementation of such a framework using JavaScript ES6 modules and Promises for asynchronous loading and execution. This example does not include all features you mentioned but it should give you an idea about how to start building such a system. 

```javascript
class ModuleLoader {
    constructor() {
        this.modules = {};
    }

    load(moduleName) {
        if (this.modules[moduleName]) {
            return Promise.resolve(this.modules[moduleName]);
        } else {
            return import(`./${moduleName}.js`).then((module) => {
                this.modules[moduleName] = module;
                return module;
            });
        }
    }
}

class App {
    constructor() {
        this.loader = new ModuleLoader();
        this.state = {};
    }

    async loadModule(moduleName) {
        const module = await this.loader.load(moduleName);
        if (typeof module.initialize === 'function') {
            await module.initialize(this.state);
        }
    }
}
```
In the above code, `ModuleLoader` is a class that manages loading and caching of modules. It uses dynamic imports to load modules asynchronously and stores them in memory for future use. 

