For serialization/deserialization, you might want to look into libraries like Google's Protocol Buffers which provide a language-agnostic way of serializing structured data. For checkpointing mechanism, you could periodically save the state of your system (including the array and any other relevant data) to disk. If an interruption occurs during this process, you can load the saved state when the system restarts. 

Remember that these are just suggestions and the actual implementation will depend on many factors such as the expected workload characteristics, the specific requirements of your application, and the constraints of your environment.
