['Here is an example of how you might implement this in C# using async/await to handle I/O operations efficiently and Task Parallel Library (TPL) for concurrency. This code assumes that the existing logging framework supports asynchronous operations and has a method `LogAsync(string logEntry)` for processing each log entry:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class LogProcessor
{
    private readonly Func<string, bool> filterCriteria;
    private readonly ILoggingFramework loggingFramework;

    public LogProcessor(Func<string, bool> filterCriteria, ILoggingFramework loggingFramework)
    {
        this.filterCriteria = filterCriteria ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(filterCriteria));
        this.loggingFramework = loggingFramework ?? throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(loggingFramework));
    }

    public async Task<List<string>> ProcessLogFileAsync(string filePath)
    {
        var filteredEntries = new List<string>();

        using (var reader = File.OpenText(filePath))
        {
            string line;
            while ((line = await reader.ReadLineAsync()) != null)
            {
                if (filterCriteria(line))
                {
                    filteredEntries.Add(line);
                    await loggingFramework.LogAsync(line);
                }
            }
        }

        return filteredEntries;
    }
}
```
This code reads the log file line by line, applying the filter criteria to each line and adding it to a list if it passes. It also logs each entry using the provided logging framework asynchronously. This approach minimizes memory usage by processing the file in chunks rather than loading the entire file into memory at once.

Please note that this is a basic example and may need adjustments based on your specific requirements, such as error handling or different log file structures. Also, please ensure to replace `ILoggingFramework` with your actual logging framework interface.
